  The words on the bundle's one page (WixStdBA's licence-link theme), spec 112 task T19. Only the two strings that
  say what the bundle does differ from WixStdBA's own: the paragraph, whose link is Microsoft's licence terms
  (the bundle's LicenseUrl), and the box that accepts them. ASCII only.
-->
<WixLocalization Culture="en-us" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/wix/2006/localization">
  <String Id="InstallLicenseLinkText">If this computer has no Microsoft C++ build tools, setup first downloads and installs them from Microsoft (roughly 1.5 GB to download and 6 GB on disk), then installs PowerRustCOBOL AI. Microsoft's &lt;a href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;license terms&lt;/a&gt; apply to them.</String>
  <String Id="InstallAcceptCheckbox">I accept Microsoft's &amp;license terms</String>
</WixLocalization>
